=begin pod

=head1 NAME

L10N::HU - Hungarian localization of Raku

=head1 SYNOPSIS

=begin output
$ hunku -e 'mond "Helló Világ"'
Helló Világ
=end output

=begin code :lang<raku>
# Must have RAKUDO_RAKUAST=1 environment variable set
# when running a Rakudo older than the 2026.09 release
use L10N::HU;
mond "Helló Világ";
=end code

=head1 DESCRIPTION

The C<L10N::HU> distribution contains the logic to provide a Hungarian
localization of the Raku Programming Language.  It installs a
C<hunku> executable that will automatically activate the Hungarian
localization.  And it allows one to use the Hungarian localization
in selected programs with a C<use L10N::HU> statement.

